    description: "WHAT, after PR #2200 gave stable_id / shape_id / repo_fingerprint values a label derived from their scheme constant:\n- 506 lines in 97 test files pin an id with the label written out (`hgstableid15:<hex>`, `hgshapeid4:`, `hgrepofp3:`). Every future scheme bump changes the label of EVERY value, so every one of those lines must be rewritten even when its digest did not move. PR #2200 did it with a throwaway script (a per-file check that the digest multiset is unchanged); no script is in the tree. Options: commit such a script, or have tests build the literal from schema.STABLE_ID_PREFIX.\n- fingerprint.py holds its own `hgfp2:` literal; it is not derived from SYMBOL_FINGERPRINT_SCHEME through schema.value_label as the other four are.\n- slice.py:374's feature id is `sha256:` (a query digest; not named in WI-talos's scope list; left).\n- The frozen text `sha256:` inside hash inputs (analyze/base.py `_NESTED_ID_HASH_LABEL`) is now part of the formula: a folded id enters another id's hash input in its v14 text. Changing it is a scheme bump. Recorded in ADR-0035 section 7; listed here so it is findable.\n- Adding the top-level `scip_stable_id_scheme` did not bump SCHEMA_VERSION (folded into the unreleased 0.21.0, as `request_ingress` was). If the owner wants 0.21.1, that is one constant.\n\nFound during PR 2 of the stable-id plan (the v15 bump), 2026-11-16 (PR #2200). Detail: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/stable_id_items_review_11152026/pr2/STATUS.md."  # c124
    fields: {}  # c124
